# Driving the raft (docs/design/raft-scene-feedback.md Phase D): E at the helm
# takes the wheel, W/D then steer the raft instead of walking the player.

case KeyW does not move the raft without the helm interaction
start walk raft
click
lock
stand helm
mark
down KeyW
frame 50 x10
expect driving = false
expect raft.moved < 0.5

case E at the helm drives, W moves the raft along its heading
start walk raft
click
lock
stand helm
press KeyE
frame 50 x2
expect driving = true
mark
down KeyW
frame 50 x10
expect raft.heading = 0
expect raft.moved > 0.8

case D turns the raft
start walk raft
click
lock
stand helm
press KeyE
frame 50 x2
expect driving = true
down KeyD
frame 50 x10
up KeyD
frame 50 x2
expect raft.heading != 0

case E again leaves the helm and W walks the player
start walk raft
click
lock
stand helm
press KeyE
frame 50 x2
expect driving = true
press KeyE
frame 50 x2
expect driving = false
mark
down KeyW
frame 50 x10
expect raft.moved < 0.5
expect moved > 0.5

# Not covered here: the raft stopping against a solid block. The DSL has no
# step for placing a block at the raft's height, and the Rust tests cover the stop.
